<title>FINLAND: FINNISH BANKS' MARKKA LENDING DOWN IN MAY - C.BANK.</title>
<headline>FINNISH BANKS' MARKKA LENDING DOWN IN MAY - C.BANK.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banks' new lending to the</p>
<p>public fell in May to 8.9 billion markka from 12.1 billion in</p>
<p>April, the Bank of Finland said in its monthly financial markets</p>
<p>review received on Monday.</p>
<p>The stock of credits at the end of May was 265.5 billion, up</p>
<p>from 264.1 billion a month earlier, it said.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures:</p>
<p>Finnish banks' markka credits (FIM bln unless stated):</p>
<p>						 May	 April</p>
<p> Total new credits			8.87	 12.11</p>
<p>  avge interest rate		   4.96%	 4.64%</p>
<p> Stock of credits to public	 265.47	264.05</p>
<p>  avge interest rate		   5.62%	 5.65%</p>
<p> New credits to households	    4.13	  4.19</p>
<p>  avge interest rate		   5.89%	 5.95%</p>
<p> Stock of credits to households    152.5	 151.9</p>
<p>  avge interest rate		   6.25%	 6.28%</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
